    "result": "I implemented `plan_extraction` in `solution.py`, keeping the stub's `UnsafePathError(ValueError)` class and function signature. The function validates `dest` and then each member: it rejects NUL characters, absolute paths, drive prefixes, and anything that climbs above the destination, including members that become empty after normalisation. Backslashes count as separators, `..` is only special when it is exactly two dots, and directory entries are validated but left out of the result. Duplicate targets are rejected case-insensitively, and any error raises before a list is returned, so no partial plan comes back. I wrote 34 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py` covering these rules, and `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all of them. I edited only `solution.py` and files inside `tests/`, and installed nothing.",
